1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Make money while we’re training?

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:05,000
At the Heavens Arena.

3
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:08,000
Heavens Arena…?

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:10,000
Yeah! I’ll explain later.

5
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:12,000
But we really ought to get going now!

6
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,000
[Gon] Right!

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,000
[theme song playing]

8
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:47,000
Whoa! Look, it’s huge!

9
00:01:47,000 --> 00:01:48,000
Yep.

10
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:50,000
That’s Heavens Arena.

11
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:52,000
It’s two 251 stories,

12
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:54,000
and 991 meters tall,

13
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:57,000
making it the world’s fourth
tallest building.

14
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:00,000
So, this is where we’ll be training…

15
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:07,000
Well, the tickets
we bought to get us here,

16
00:02:07,000 --> 00:02:09,000
left us completely broke.

17
00:02:09,000 --> 00:02:11,000
We’ve gotta make more while we’re here.

18
00:02:11,000 --> 00:02:13,000
We’ll start fresh when we disembark.

19
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:15,000
Right! I got it.

20
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,000
All right. Well? Let’s go!

21
00:02:17,000 --> 00:02:19,000
[Gon] Okay!

22
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:24,000
ARRIVAL x AT x THE ARENA

23
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,000
[narrator] Gon and Killua
head to Heavens Arena

24
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:29,000
with only one goal in mind:

25
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,000
to get stronger.

26
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:32,000
[Killua] Gon.

27
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,000
[Gon] This is a really long line.

28
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Is everyone going to Heavens Arena?

29
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:42,000
There aren’t any rules to worry about.

30
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:44,000
Not like there were for the Hunter Exam.

31
00:02:44,000 --> 00:02:46,000
You just gotta knock your opponent out.

32
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,000
Oh…

33
00:02:48,000 --> 00:02:51,000
The higher you go,
the more prize money you make.

34
00:02:52,000 --> 00:02:54,000
If you want to earn a living
with your fists,

35
00:02:54,000 --> 00:02:56,000
this is as good as it gets!

36
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:58,000
[receptionist] Welcome to Heavens Arena.

37
00:02:59,000 --> 00:03:01,000
Now, if you wouldn’t mind
filling out this form…

38
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:09,000
Killua Zoldyck, you’re number 2054.

39
00:03:09,000 --> 00:03:12,000
Gon Freecss, you are 2055.

40
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,000
On the first arena floor,

41
00:03:14,000 --> 00:03:16,000
they’ll be calling you by your number,

42
00:03:16,000 --> 00:03:17,000
so try not to forget it.

43
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,000
Please go on ahead.

44
00:03:22,000 --> 00:03:25,000
[cheering]

45
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,000
Wow…!

46
00:03:32,000 --> 00:03:34,000
[grunting]

47
00:03:36,000 --> 00:03:38,000
-Looking good!
-Do it!

48
00:03:39,000 --> 00:03:40,000
It's been a while,

49
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:42,000
but the place hasn't changed.

50
00:03:42,000 --> 00:03:44,000
Wait… you mean you’ve been here before?

51
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:47,000
Yeah. When I was about six.

52
00:03:47,000 --> 00:03:49,000
My dad left me here flat broke.

53
00:03:50,000 --> 00:03:52,000
Told me to reach 200th floor.

54
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Took me two whole years.

55
00:03:55,000 --> 00:03:56,000
Two years?

56
00:03:56,000 --> 00:03:58,000
I mean, sure, he was only six…

57
00:03:58,000 --> 00:04:00,000
but it took him that long?

58
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,000
There are guys of Hisoka’s caliber

59
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:05,000
but only farther up, so don’t waste time.

60
00:04:05,000 --> 00:04:07,000
-Ya got it?
-Uh-huh.

61
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:12,000
[announcer] Numbers 1973 and 2055.

62
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:13,000
to ring E.

63
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:16,000
2055! That's me!

64
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:19,000
Oh, man, I’m getting pretty nervous
right about now.

65
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Gon. You made it
through the Testing Gate, right?

66
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:23,000
Hm?

67
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,000
So, relax.

68
00:04:26,000 --> 00:04:28,000
[man 1] Check it out! It’s just a kid!

69
00:04:29,000 --> 00:04:32,000
[man 2] Hey!
Ya better run while you still can, kid!

70
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:34,000
[man 3] This ain’t a game!

71
00:04:34,000 --> 00:04:37,000
Give him a punch and send him flying!

72
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:41,000
This is a first-floor fight

73
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:43,000
so we will be appraising
your skill levels.

74
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:45,000
You’re allowed three minutes
to demonstrate

75
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,000
what you’re capable of.

76
00:04:49,000 --> 00:04:51,000
Now then… Begin!

77
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
-I’m real sorry, kid.
-[flexing knuckles]

78
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:55,000
But I’ll make it fast,
so you don’t have to suffer!

79
00:04:57,000 --> 00:04:59,000
You made it
through the Testing Gate, right?

80
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:03,000
So, relax! Go out there and push hard!

81
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:04,000
Okay, so just…

82
00:05:05,000 --> 00:05:06,000
push hard!

83
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
[screams]

84
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:12,000
No way!

85
00:05:12,000 --> 00:05:13,000
Nice!

86
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:15,000
[impressed callouts]

87
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:17,000
[man 2] That kid’s incredible!

88
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:19,000
[man 1] What crazy power!

89
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:22,000
When did I get so strong?

90
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:29,000
2055, proceed directly to floor 50.

91
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,000
Okay!

92
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:35,000
[impressed callouts]

93
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:37,000
[man 2] Look at that!

94
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:40,000
That first kid’s not the only one
who’s a beast!

95
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
[beeping]

96
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Wait.

97
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:46,000
This says you’ve already been
to the 200th floor?

98
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
And those were some powerful moves.

99
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:51,000
All right. Go to the 180th floor--

100
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Nah. I’ll start at 50.

101
00:05:52,000 --> 00:05:53,000
[referee] Huh?

102
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,000
I want to take it slow.

103
00:05:57,000 --> 00:05:59,000
[impressed callouts]

104
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:03,000
[referee] Enough!

105
00:06:04,000 --> 00:06:06,000
[man 1]
Whoa! That kid’s pretty powerful, too!

106
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:12,000
You’re permitted to advance
to the 50th floor.

107
00:06:13,000 --> 00:06:14,000
Osu! Thank you!

108
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
[female guide]
The first 200 floors of Heavens Arena

109
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:24,000
are divided into classes, ten floors each.

110
00:06:25,000 --> 00:06:28,000
Which means that a fighter
who wins on the 50th floor,

111
00:06:28,000 --> 00:06:29,000
advances to the 60th.

112
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:34,000
Lose and they automatically drop down
to the 40th floor.

113
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:35,000
[Gon] So that’s how it works…

114
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:37,000
[Killua] Also…

115
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:40,000
I’ve heard once you get all the way
to the 100th floor,

116
00:06:40,000 --> 00:06:41,000
they comp you your very own room!

117
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:45,000
Oh! I’m sorry, how impolite!

118
00:06:46,000 --> 00:06:48,000
Osu! My name is Zushi!

119
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:50,000
And you?

120
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:51,000
I'm Killua.

121
00:06:51,000 --> 00:06:52,000
My name’s Gon.

122
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,000
Nice to meet you.

123
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:56,000
-[elevator dings]
-[guide] Here we are.

124
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:01,000
[Zushi] Oh, I watched your fights earlier.

125
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:02,000
You guys are amazing!

126
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,000
What are you talking about?

127
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:07,000
You made it up here
with only one match, too.

128
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:08,000
He’s right!

129
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,000
No, no.

130
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:11,000
I still have a long way to go.

131
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:13,000
By the way,
what discipline do you practice?

132
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:16,000
I study the Shingen-ryu technique.

133
00:07:17,000 --> 00:07:19,000
A discipline? Don’t have one.

134
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:20,000
Nope.

135
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:21,000
You’re kidding!

136
00:07:21,000 --> 00:07:24,000
You’re both that powerful
with no formal training?

137
00:07:25,000 --> 00:07:27,000
I’m humbled to be in your presence.

138
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:29,000
I’ve come a long way,
but I’m not finished!

139
00:07:29,000 --> 00:07:30,000
[someone clapping their hands.]

140
00:07:31,000 --> 00:07:32,000
[man] Zushi!

141
00:07:33,000 --> 00:07:34,000
You did well.

142
00:07:34,000 --> 00:07:35,000
Thank you, Master!

143
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:38,000
I’m very happy to see
that you stuck to my teachings.

144
00:07:40,000 --> 00:07:41,000
Osu! I am honored.

145
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:44,000
But Master your shirt’s untucked.

146
00:07:45,000 --> 00:07:46,000
Oh! Sorry about that.

147
00:07:47,000 --> 00:07:48,000
[nervous giggle]

148
00:07:48,000 --> 00:07:49,000
Who are they?

149
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:51,000
Oh. This is Killua and Gon.

150
00:07:52,000 --> 00:07:54,000
Pleasure to meet you.
My name is Wing.

151
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:56,000
[both] Osu!

152
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,000
I really wasn’t expecting
to see any other kids here

153
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,000
besides Zushi.

154
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:02,000
So, what brings the two of you here?

155
00:08:02,000 --> 00:08:03,000
Uh, we--

156
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:05,000
well, we want to become stronger.

157
00:08:06,000 --> 00:08:07,000
But we’re also pretty broke,

158
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:10,000
so we’re making money
at exactly the same time.

159
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:12,000
Yeah. Killua’s been here before, sir.

160
00:08:13,000 --> 00:08:14,000
That right?

161
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:15,000
You must be quite talented

162
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:17,000
or else you wouldn’t have made it
to this level.

163
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,000
Even so, pay close attention

164
00:08:19,000 --> 00:08:22,000
to your opponent’s body and your own.

165
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:23,000
[both] Osu!

166
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:28,000
[female staffer]
Killua, Gon, and Zushi. Ah, there we are.

167
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Hand me your tickets, please.

168
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:37,000
Here. This is your prize money
from the earlier fight.

169
00:08:40,000 --> 00:08:42,000
152 jenny...

170
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:48,000
On this floor, you make just enough
for a juice, win or lose.

171
00:08:48,000 --> 00:08:50,000
But on all of the other floors here

172
00:08:50,000 --> 00:08:52,000
a loss gets you nothing.

173
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:55,000
Winning on the 50th floor
earns fifty thousand.

174
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:56,000
Fifty thousand?!

175
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,000
That’s a lot of money!

176
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:01,000
The 100th floor,
I think you get a million.

177
00:09:02,000 --> 00:09:05,000
Once you're past the 150th floor,
you get ten million.

178
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Ten million?

179
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:10,000
Didn’t you make it to 200th floor before?

180
00:09:10,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Whoa! The 200th floor?

181
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:15,000
[Gon] How much do you get
for winning on the 200th floor?

182
00:09:16,000 --> 00:09:18,000
To tell the truth,
I don’t actually know that.

183
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:21,000
because I quit pretty
much as soon as I qualified for it.

184
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:24,000
But when I won on the 190th floor,

185
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:26,000
I had around 200 million in total.

186
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:28,000
Two hundred...

187
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Where's that money now?

188
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:31,000
[Killua] That was four years ago,

189
00:09:32,000 --> 00:09:33,000
so it’s long gone by now.

190
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:35,000
I spent all of it on snacks!

191
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:37,000
That much on snacks in four years?

192
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:39,000
What kind of snacks were they?

193
00:09:41,000 --> 00:09:43,000
Hey. Let’s head up to the waiting room.

194
00:09:43,000 --> 00:09:45,000
We got through our matches unscathed
on the first floor.

195
00:09:46,000 --> 00:09:48,000
They’ll probably give us
another one today.

196
00:09:59,000 --> 00:10:01,000
Well, if these guys are our opponents,

197
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:02,000
it’ll be a cinch.

198
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:04,000
Just take it easy.

199
00:10:04,000 --> 00:10:05,000
Really?

200
00:10:05,000 --> 00:10:07,000
-Killua!
-[quiet grumble]

201
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:09,000
Quiet! They can hear you!

202
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,000
[announcer] 2054, Mister Killua.

203
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:14,000
Hey, I’m already up.

204
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:17,000
[announcer] And 1963, Mister Zushi.

205
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,000
Huh?!

206
00:10:18,000 --> 00:10:21,000
[announcer]
Please head to Arena A on the 57th floor.

207
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:24,000
Okay.

208
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
Osu! I am honored to face you!

209
00:10:27,000 --> 00:10:29,000
I bet. Well, you can’t win ‘em all.

210
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Better luck next time, right?

211
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:32,000
Catch ya later, Gon.

212
00:10:32,000 --> 00:10:35,000
Yeah. Best of luck to both of you guys!

213
00:10:36,000 --> 00:10:38,000
I’ll wait on the floor above. Bye.

214
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,000
[Gon] ‘kay!

215
00:10:42,000 --> 00:10:45,000
He didn’t have to act
like it was such a done deal.

216
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:48,000
[commentator] All right, everyone!

217
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:50,000
This is the event
you’ve all been waiting for!

218
00:10:50,000 --> 00:10:52,000
A unique match-up between two young boys

219
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:55,000
who’ve both got something to prove!

220
00:10:55,000 --> 00:10:58,000
But don’t underestimate these fighters!

221
00:10:58,000 --> 00:11:00,000
Both had strong showings
in their first rounds

222
00:11:00,000 --> 00:11:04,000
and now they’ve jumped all the way up here
to the 50th floor!

223
00:11:05,000 --> 00:11:06,000
ZUSHI - KILLUA

224
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:08,000
And now let’s take a look
at the big screen

225
00:11:08,000 --> 00:11:10,000
for the playback of those events!

226
00:11:11,000 --> 00:11:13,000
Killua beat his opponent in a flash!

227
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:17,000
One chop was all it took to knock him out!

228
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:23,000
Zushi used martial arts
to punish his opponent

229
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,000
scoring a flawless knockout

230
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,000
against a giant weighing
over 200 kilograms!

231
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,000
Okay now, everyone!

232
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Ready to press your wager buttons?

233
00:11:35,000 --> 00:11:37,000
Go on! Make your picks right now!

234
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:41,000
[jingle]

235
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:45,000
[commentator] All the bets are in,
and we have a clear favorite! Zushi!

236
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:46,000
[irked grumble]

237
00:11:47,000 --> 00:11:50,000
[commentator] Maybe his knowledge
of martial arts has given him the edge!

238
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
[Zushi] This isn’t good…

239
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:53,000
Killua is mad.

240
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,000
Three rounds!

241
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Three minutes per round
decided by points or K.O.!

242
00:11:59,000 --> 00:11:59,000
Begin!

243
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:04,000
[Killua] I see.

244
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:07,000
His stance doesn’t leave many openings.

245
00:12:07,000 --> 00:12:09,000
He’s trained hard to master it.

246
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:12,000
But he doesn’t stand a chance against me.

247
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:17,000
[commentator] Wow! Killua is walking
boldly toward his opponent!

248
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:21,000
[strangled cry]

249
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:25,000
[Killua] Sorry, but I’m sticking
to one chop per match

250
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:27,000
‘til I reach the 150th floor.

251
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:30,000
A clean hit!

252
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:35,000
[commentator] Killua has laid out
another opponent with a single blow!

253
00:12:35,000 --> 00:12:38,000
A clean hit and a knockout
earn him two points!

254
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:41,000
As you know
under the points and knockout system,

255
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:45,000
there are clean hits,
critical hits, and knockdowns.

256
00:12:46,000 --> 00:12:49,000
Great attacks count as ‘clean hits’,
worth one point each.

257
00:12:49,000 --> 00:12:51,000
Superb attacks are ‘critical hits’,

258
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:53,000
and are worth two points.

259
00:12:53,000 --> 00:12:55,000
Knocking your opponent down is one point.

260
00:12:56,000 --> 00:12:59,000
Collect ten points and you’re awarded
a technical knockout.

261
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:02,000
Of course, if your opponent
can’t continue the fight after one hit

262
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:04,000
you win by knockout!

263
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,000
[Killua] Pretty sure that chop ended it.
Idiot.

264
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:09,000
Can you fight?

265
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:11,000
Yes! I’m all right!

266
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:14,000
[commentator] He got up!

267
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,000
Zushi will continue the match!

268
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,000
And begin!

269
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:22,000
[Killua] Did I hold back too much?

270
00:13:23,000 --> 00:13:24,000
[Zushi grunting]

271
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:26,000
[Zushi roars]

272
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:28,000
[cries out]

273
00:13:29,000 --> 00:13:30,000
[commentator] He’s taken another hit!

274
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:32,000
Zushi is down!

275
00:13:33,000 --> 00:13:35,000
But he’s getting up
before the referee reaches him,

276
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:38,000
meaning Killua won’t be awarded the point!

277
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:41,000
[grunts] He’s good.

278
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:44,000
I’ll have to change my tactics.

279
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:48,000
But something’s not right.

280
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:50,000
That attack was so strong

281
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:52,000
that even if I just grazed him,
he’d be out cold.

282
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,000
[Zushi] Unbelievable!

283
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:58,000
Such awesome power and speed!

284
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,000
At this rate, I won’t stand a chance!

285
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:04,000
But I’ve gotta try.

286
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,000
I have to!

287
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:30,000
[commentator] Uh-oh! What’s happening?

288
00:14:30,000 --> 00:14:32,000
It looks like Killua is on the run!

289
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:34,000
[yells] Zushi!

290
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:52,000
[commentator] So...

291
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:54,000
a very loud and overenthusiastic spectator

292
00:14:55,000 --> 00:14:56,000
has temporarily interrupted the fight

293
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:59,000
but let’s see
if we can get it going again!

294
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,000
Come on folks, whaddya say?

295
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:04,000
ELEVATOR

296
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:05,000
[elevator dings]

297
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:08,000
Oh, hey! Killua!
Over here!

298
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:12,000
Check it out! I got 60000.

299
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,000
How about you?

300
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:16,000
It took you longer to get here
than I expected.

301
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,000
Yeah, I ran into some trouble.

302
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:22,000
So, was Zushi pretty strong?
Or what?

303
00:15:22,000 --> 00:15:24,000
No way… No.

304
00:15:25,000 --> 00:15:26,000
He has potential.

305
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:28,000
He’ll be strong one day.

306
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:29,000
For now, anyway,

307
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,000
he’s just target practice for me.

308
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
Punches that weak,

309
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,000
I could knock him around easy.

310
00:15:37,000 --> 00:15:39,000
But I couldn’t beat him.

311
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,000
Huh?

312
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,000
I won the match.

313
00:15:42,000 --> 00:15:43,000
TKO by points.

314
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:46,000
But still I just couldn’t knock him out.

315
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:48,000
Also…

316
00:15:49,000 --> 00:15:51,000
When he changed his stance,

317
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:53,000
I got this real creepy feeling,

318
00:15:53,000 --> 00:15:55,000
like when I face my brother.

319
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
I don't know what it was,

320
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,000
but it felt... dangerous.

321
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
It’s gotta be some kind of technique.

322
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,000
I heard his master

323
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:10,000
call it ‘Ren’.

324
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
[Zushi] Please! Forgive me, Master!

325
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:17,000
[Wing] I thought I made it clear to you

326
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:20,000
that you were not supposed
to use Ren yet, Zushi.

327
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:24,000
[Zushi] I’m sorry!
It’s just... he-- he was so strong,

328
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,000
I couldn't help myself.

329
00:16:27,000 --> 00:16:30,000
Yes. I understand the urge to win.

330
00:16:30,000 --> 00:16:31,000
But you have another goal.

331
00:16:32,000 --> 00:16:33,000
A goal that lies beyond this.

332
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,000
At the top floor of this tower.

333
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Don’t focus too much
on simply winning, Zushi.

334
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Impatience will only erode your potential.

335
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:44,000
Osu!

336
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:48,000
You must be prepared to lose
a thousand times while you’re here.

337
00:16:48,000 --> 00:16:49,000
[Zushi] Osu!

338
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:53,000
So, he’s not supposed to use Ren?

339
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Until he gets all the way up
to the top floor, I mean?

340
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,000
That’s where
the strongest fighters are, right?

341
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:01,000
At the top?

342
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Gon. We need to change our plan.

343
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Huh?

344
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:09,000
I say we shoot for the top floor.

345
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Right!

346
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:17,000
Actually, that’s been my plan
this whole time!

347
00:17:23,000 --> 00:17:25,000
-[crowd cheering]
-[fighter grunts]

348
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:27,000
[commentator]
Killua defeats another opponent

349
00:17:27,000 --> 00:17:29,000
with one chop for a knockout win!

350
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:32,000
Now there’s action over in the next arena.

351
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:36,000
Gon has knocked out another opponent
with a single push!

352
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:40,000
Each of them has won
six consecutive matches

353
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:41,000
over the past three days,

354
00:17:41,000 --> 00:17:44,000
And they’ve reached the hundreds
without even a scratch to show for it!

355
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,000
[jingle]

356
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:48,000
Killua's chop.

357
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,000
and Gon’s push.

358
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:51,000
They seem unstoppable.

359
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:53,000
But can they keep it up?

360
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,000
But the real question is

361
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:58,000
who if anyone can stop them?

362
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Yay! Our own room!

363
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:08,000
[laughing]

364
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:11,000
We’re not gonna have to worry
about money and lodging anymore!

365
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:13,000
I wouldn’t be so sure.

366
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,000
Try to remember,

367
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:17,000
drop below the 100th floor
and you lose the room.

368
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:20,000
There’s a huge difference
between getting here

369
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:22,000
and staying here on the 100th floor.

370
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,000
It’s a real threshold.

371
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Threshold?

372
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:29,000
Beyond the 100th floor,
you get special treatment.

373
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:33,000
And so, naturally,
no one wants to lose their standing.

374
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:36,000
There are people here
who’ll do anything it takes

375
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,000
to stay on the 100th floor.

376
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:41,000
You can waste a lot of time on ‘em.

377
00:18:41,000 --> 00:18:43,000
Time we don’t have right now.

378
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:45,000
So be careful, Gon.

379
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:51,000
[crowd cheering]

380
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:55,000
[commentator]
Gon wins another match with a single push!

381
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:58,000
[Killua]
Guess I didn’t need to worry about him.

382
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:08,000
[crowd cheering]

383
00:19:09,000 --> 00:19:12,000
Your prize money has been deposited
into your account.

384
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:15,000
[Gon] You were right.

385
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:17,000
I've never seen so many zeros before.

386
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:21,000
Crazy that just last week,
I was totally broke.

387
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,000
I’m a little bit annoyed.

388
00:19:25,000 --> 00:19:26,000
Huh?

389
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,000
The first time I was here,

390
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:31,000
it took me two whole months
to reach floor 150.

391
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:33,000
You, on the other hand...

392
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:36,000
Yeah, but back then, you were only six.

393
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Well yeah, there’s that.

394
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,000
[Gon] Oh, by the way,

395
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:43,000
I saw Zushi on TV earlier.

396
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:45,000
[Killua] Yeah, so did I.

397
00:19:45,000 --> 00:19:46,000
He’s still on the 50th floor.

398
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,000
I wonder what that ‘Ren’ thing was
that creeped you out.

399
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,000
And why.

400
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:56,000
[Killua] It’s weird, huh?

401
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:59,000
Hmm...

402
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:02,000
Maybe we’ll meet
some opponents higher up who use it.

403
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:03,000
Or maybe...

404
00:20:04,000 --> 00:20:06,000
it’d be faster to just ask Zushi!

405
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:13,000
Ren is one of the Four Exercises.

406
00:20:14,000 --> 00:20:17,000
The Four Exercises are fundamental
to all martial arts.

407
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:20,000
They instill discipline
and develop character.

408
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:25,000
“Learn Ten, know Zetsu,
through Ren to attain Hatsu!”

409
00:20:25,000 --> 00:20:28,000
And all of that is how you train for Nen!

410
00:20:28,000 --> 00:20:30,000
-That’s it!
-Start making sense!

411
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:32,000
[Wing] Zushi…

412
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:34,000
Are you certain

413
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:36,000
that you’re sufficiently qualified
to be teaching others?

414
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:39,000
Now, Gon, Killua…

415
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,000
An old proverb warns:

416
00:20:41,000 --> 00:20:44,000
that it’s possible
a smattering of knowledge

417
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:45,000
may not reduce one’s ignorance,

418
00:20:46,000 --> 00:20:47,000
but increase it.

419
00:20:48,000 --> 00:20:50,000
So, you’re saying a little knowledge
is a dangerous thing’?

420
00:20:51,000 --> 00:20:54,000
Thanks for the tip,
but I really want to learn this.

421
00:20:54,000 --> 00:20:58,000
Because I’m convinced
it’s behind my brother’s powers.

422
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:02,000
You say that your brother...

423
00:21:02,000 --> 00:21:04,000
is able to use Nen?

424
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:08,000
I need to understand
what Nen and Ren even mean!

425
00:21:09,000 --> 00:21:10,000
And not just halfway.

426
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,000
I need to know it!

427
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:14,000
If you’re willing to teach me,

428
00:21:14,000 --> 00:21:16,000
I won’t try to figure it out for myself.

429
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:25,000
Well, in that case…

430
00:21:28,000 --> 00:21:29,000
Let’s adjourn to my room.

431
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:33,000
[narrator] Questions abound.

432
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:36,000
What is Nen? What is Ren?

433
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:41,000
Killua believes they’re related
to his older brother Illumi’s abilities.

434
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:45,000
Gon wants to know
what these words mean, as well.

435
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:49,000
[theme song playing]

436
00:22:56,000 --> 00:22:57,000
[Gon] Coming up:

437
00:22:57,000 --> 00:22:58,000
-Gon...
-[Killua] ...and Killua’s…

438
00:22:58,000 --> 00:23:00,000
[Gon and Killua] Hunterpedia!

439
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:02,000
-I’m Gon!
-I’m Killua!

440
00:23:02,000 --> 00:23:04,000
[both] And this is our Hunterpedia!

441
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:06,000
Today we’ll be introducing Zushi!

442
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:08,000
He’s really, really talented.

443
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:10,000
In fact, he’s considered
one in a hundred thousand!

444
00:23:10,000 --> 00:23:12,000
While Gon and I are
one in a hundred million!

445
00:23:13,000 --> 00:23:14,000
Osu!

446
00:23:21,000 --> 00:23:22,000
[Gon] Next time:

447
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:23,000
"Nen x And x Nen."

448
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:25,000
That was a rough one!

449
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:26,000
[Killua] But you hung in there!

450
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:27,000
[both] Osu!
